
; test-cat - Chia's CAT v2 asset layer, ported to symbll and
; committed under the bll leaf version
;
; Source: puzzles/cat_puzzles/cat_v2.clsp with cat_truths.clib, and
; puzzles/cat_puzzles/genesis_by_coin_id.clsp as the issuance hook,
; from Chia-Network/chia_puzzles release 0.20.3
; (d122456feeef55708d354a065623037bfa010714). A CAT marks a set of
; UTXOs as units of one asset and enforces, at every spend, that the
; marked value entering a transaction equals the marked value
; leaving it, unless the asset's committed issuance program approves
; the difference. Each holder locks their units under their own
; spend policy without weakening the asset layer.
;
; The port keeps the source's per-holder wrapping. A holder's leaf is
; the shared asset body applied to the holder's inner program,
; assembled as
;   (a (q . BODY) (rc (q . INNER) 1))
; so the serialized leaf is PREFIX || SINNER || SUFFIX: PREFIX is
; identical for every holder of the asset and carries BODY with the
; committed constants quoted inside, SINNER is the serialization of
; the holder's quoted inner program, and SUFFIX is the constant four
; bytes 0xff018080 closing the wrapper. The witness reveals PREFIX
; once and one SINNER per claimed member, and MEMBER rebuilds the
; BIP341 output key from those bytes, which is the port's form of
; the source's curried puzzle hash reconstruction. The split is
; canonical because the committed PREFIXLEN pins the boundary, and
; the contrast section at the end of this file shows the mint that
; opens without it.
;
; The program is committed as the body of a taproot leaf under the
; bll leaf version 0xc2 and every context below is a real spend
; validated by the repl's spend command: fixed witness stack of
; environment element, leaf script and control block, canonical
; encodings, budget from the witness size, truthy result accepted.
; The witness environment element is the compiled argument tree
;   (((PREFIX . SINNERME) . (ICLAIMS . OCLAIMS)) .
;    ((PROOF . PROOF2) . ((LC . TAILR) . (TAILS . IARGS))))
; with ICLAIMS a list of (IDX SINNER . PAR) input claims, OCLAIMS a
; list of output entries consumed in output order, each either a
; (nil SINNER . PAR) member claim or a (1 V LEAF IPK PATH . PAR)
; disclaimer revealing a foreign output's taproot preimage, LC the
; (PIDX LSIN . LPAR) lineage claim, TAILR and TAILS the revealed
; issuance program and its arguments, and IARGS the inner program's
; arguments, here a signature.
;
; Block map from the source to this port:
;   MOD_HASH and puzzle-hash-of-curried-function -> PREFIX, the
;     shared serialized body, with MEMBER rebuilding each member's
;     output key from PREFIX and a revealed SINNER through the
;     TapLeaf hash and the BIP341 tweak
;   INNER_PUZZLE and inner_puzzle_solution -> the SINNER region of
;     the leaf and IARGS, applied through (a INNER IARGS)
;   TAIL_PROGRAM_HASH, the -113 magic condition and tail_solution ->
;     TAILHASH quoted in the body, the witness slots TAILR and
;     TAILS, and RUNTAIL's tree hash check before the apply. The
;     ported issuance program is genesis_by_coin_id: it approves
;     only a zero delta whose revealed parent consumed the committed
;     GENESIS outpoint at input 0
;   the announcement ring, prev_coin_id, this_coin_info,
;     next_coin_proof, prev_subtotal -> gone. The ring exists to sum
;     per-member deltas across a spend bundle, and a transaction
;     already binds its inputs and outputs atomically, so OUTSCAN
;     and INCLAIM read the real amounts and the delta is computed
;     directly, one objective sum per asset per transaction
;   extra_delta -> DELTA, the computed difference RUNTAIL hands the
;     issuance program
;   morph_condition and cat_puzzle_hash -> the OUTSCAN entry check,
;     every odd output must rebuild from PREFIX and a claimed
;     SINNER, or reveal its foreign preimage through DISCLAIM
;   lineage_proof and is_parent_cat -> LC with PROOF and PROOF2,
;     revealed transaction bytes in place of claimed coin id
;     components
;   cat_truths.clib -> not ported, the introspection opcodes hand
;     the program the same facts the truths struct threads
;
; Deviations, each with its reason:
;   1. Member outputs are marked by odd amounts, the singleton
;      port's convention. Chia attributes each created output to the
;      member whose program emitted it, and a transaction has no
;      such attribution: an output's membership must be decidable by
;      every input's run from the transaction alone, or an output at
;      a member script could ride along unverified and later spends
;      would accept it as backing, an unbounded mint. Odd amounts
;      make membership objective: every odd output must be claimed
;      as a member or disclaimed as proven foreign, even outputs are
;      ignored, and the port's asset units are therefore
;      denominated in satoshis with even change passing through
;      freely.
;   2. Conservation is one transaction wide equation instead of a
;      ring of per-member subtotals. Each member input's run
;      computes the same objective odd output sum, so a run that
;      under-claims its inputs fails its own equation and a run
;      that omits a member input leaves that input's own run, which
;      its script forces, to refuse. One exhibited member input in
;      the parent transaction therefore carries the whole induction.
;   3. Every odd output must be claimed as a member or disclaimed by
;      revealing its actual taproot preimage and showing it is not
;      one, so each asset's run partitions the odd outputs into its
;      own members and proven foreigners. Two assets therefore
;      compose in one transaction, the cross-asset swap the offer
;      flow needs, at the price of the foreign leaf bytes riding the
;      witness. The residue: an odd output whose script cannot be
;      revealed this way, a key path or untweaked output, cannot
;      share a transaction with the asset, so plain payments and
;      change beside a CAT use even amounts by convention.
;   4. The issuance program refuses every nonzero delta, following
;      the pinned genesis_by_coin_id. Supply is therefore fixed by
;      the odd member outputs of the one transaction that consumes
;      the GENESIS outpoint: no melt, no later issuance, member
;      spends contribute nothing to fees, and fees ride co-spent
;      unmarked inputs. Value can still be frozen, by paying a
;      member script an even amount, by an unspendable SINNER
;      region, or by an unbacked donation, and every such freeze
;      costs only its payer.
;   5. The lineage proof reveals whole transactions, the singleton
;      port's shape: PROOF must hash to my prevout txid, PROOF2 to
;      the txid in PROOF's input PIDX, and the output PROOF2 names
;      there must be an odd member. The claimed member's SINNER and
;      output key parity ride the lineage claim LC, since a foreign
;      output key's parity is not computable in the program.
;   6. Every membership claim carries the member's output key parity
;      bit as witness data, and a wrong bit only refuses the spend
;      through the muladd. The executing input's own parity is not
;      claimed, its leaf hash is pinned to (tx 6) directly.
;   7. Amounts and index fields are raw fixed width little endian,
;      not minimal integers. Parity reads the low byte through ODD8,
;      claim indices normalize through (+ X 0) and must strictly
;      increase, and the sums add raw amounts, whose numeric reading
;      is width independent.
;   8. Proof parsing accepts only canonical single byte counts below
;      0x80, enforced by RD1 as in the singleton port, and the
;      issuance program guards the one count byte it reads the same
;      way. The same recorded restriction on revealed ancestors
;      follows.
;   9. The apply surface takes exactly two operands, and the inner
;      and issuance programs are written in numeric bll opcodes,
;      both following the p2d port.
;  10. The committed region imports lib-taproot whole, so SIGNMSG
;      rides into every leaf as unreached bytes. One vetted copy of
;      the reconstruction defs outweighs a split of the library, a
;      recorded exception to the region's no dead bytes doctrine.
;
; Everything after the program marker below is the verbatim output of
;   python3 examples/gen-test-context.py cat
; which compiles the committed body from the sentinel delimited
; region below, asserts the PREFIXLEN and TAILHASH fixed points,
; assembles each holder's leaf from the shared PREFIX, validates
; every emitted spend against the real validator before printing it,
; and emits the contexts with their verdict markers, so the region
; is the single source of truth for the committed bytes and
; regeneration is a byte comparison. The chain is genesis outpoint
; -> genesis transaction -> context A -> context B, with the later
; contexts respending the same outputs in mutually exclusive
; hypotheticals, a differential section evaluating the same defs
; through the symbolic evaluator, and a contrast section showing the
; boundary shift mint the committed PREFIXLEN refuses.
;
; Run with
;   python3 examples/run-examples.py examples/test-cat
; which checks every "; expect:" marker below, or interactively with
;   echo "import examples/test-cat" | ./bllsh

; -------------------------------------------------------------------
; the committed body. Everything between the sentinel lines compiles
; into BODY, the shared half of every holder's leaf, and the
; generator re-reads exactly this region to derive the committed
; bytes, so the program marker after the region and the spend lines
; stay tied to these defs.

; --- committed program ---

; the shared commitment exclusivity pair and the taproot
; reconstruction defs, one vetted copy each for the whole corpus
import examples/lib-exclusivity
import examples/lib-taproot

; the committed constants, quoted into the body where the taproot
; commitment binds them for every holder of the asset alike
def GENESIS 0x000102030405060708090a0b0c0d0e0f101112131415161718191a1b1c1d1e1f00000000
; the tree hash of the issuance program, genesis_by_coin_id's port:
; (all (notall 2) (<s (substr 5 (q . 4) (q . 5)) (q . 0x80))
;      (= (substr 5 (q . 5) (q . 41)) (q . GENESIS)))
; over the argument tree (DELTA PROOF . TS), DELTA at 2 and PROOF at
; 5: a truthy verdict needs a zero delta and a revealed parent whose
; input 0 consumed GENESIS, with the parent's input count byte
; canonical below 0x80
def TAILHASH 0xb61928788efbb9c9fc6a6dbc633a6158bb52a1b9a4b22a90357d0a4c71699395
; the byte length of PREFIX, the committed half of every leaf. The
; constant pins the split the witness reveals: without it a spender
; could shift the boundary and rebuild members that share only a
; shorter prefix, programs this body never vetted
def PREFIXLEN 3538

; parity of a raw 8 byte little endian amount. Non-empty zero atoms
; are truthy, so the low byte is masked and compared byte exactly,
; and the empty atom is refused rather than misread as odd, the &
; fold passes an operand through when the other side is empty.
def (ODD8 A) (all (strlen A) (= (& (substr A 0 1) 1) 1))

; a single byte count or length read from revealed transaction bytes,
; canonical form only: exactly one byte, below 0x80, returned as a
; minimal int. An out of range read yields the empty atom from substr
; and must raise, not parse as zero.
def (RD1B B) (if (all (<s B 0x80) (strlen B)) (+ B 0) (x "cat: varint"))
def (RD1 P POS) (RD1B (substr P POS (+ POS 1)))

; cursor arithmetic over a serialized transaction without witness:
; an input is a 36 byte outpoint, a length prefixed scriptSig and a
; 4 byte sequence, an output is an 8 byte value and a length prefixed
; scriptPubKey
def (SKIPINS P C N) (if N (SKIPINS P (+ C 41 (RD1 P (+ C 36))) (- N 1)) C)
def (PREVOUTAT P C) (substr P C (+ C 36))
def (OUTPOS P C N) (if N (OUTPOS P (+ C 9 (RD1 P (+ C 8))) (- N 1)) C)

; the tree hash RUNTAIL checks the revealed issuance program
; against: leaves hash under a 1 tag, pairs under a 2 tag
def (SHA256TREE T) (if (l T) (sha256 2 (SHA256TREE (h T)) (SHA256TREE (t T))) (sha256 1 T))

; a positive int in [128, 32767] encodes as exactly two little
; endian bytes, so padding and truncating yields the fixed widths
; the compact size encoding needs
def (LE16 N) (substr (cat N 0x0000) 0 2)
def (CSIZE N) (if (< N 253) (substr (cat N 0x00) 0 1) (cat 0xfd (LE16 N)))

; the BIP341 leaf hash of any revealed leaf under any leaf version,
; and the member form, PREFIX || SINNER || SUFFIX under the bll leaf
; version. The generator asserts every leaf stays below the 0xfd00
; compact size boundary LE16 covers.
def (HASHTAPLEAF V LEAF) (TAGHASH "TapLeaf" (cat V (CSIZE (strlen LEAF)) LEAF))
def (HASHLEAF PREFIX SINNER) (HASHTAPLEAF 0xc2 (cat PREFIX SINNER 0xff018080))

; SPK is a member of this asset with inner serialization SINNER and
; output key parity PAR: the leaf rebuilt from the shared PREFIX
; must reach SPK's output key under the unspendable internal key
; with no siblings, the port's curried puzzle hash reconstruction.
; The muladd raises on a mismatch, so a false claim refuses the
; spend rather than returning a verdict.
def (MEMBER PREFIX SINNER PAR SPK) (TAPROOT PAR (HASHLEAF PREFIX SINNER) 0 (UNSPENDABLEIPK) (CHECKTAPSPK SPK))

; an odd output outside the asset: the disclaimer reveals the
; output's actual taproot preimage, rebuilds its output key from it,
; and shows the revealed leaf is not a member, a different leaf
; version or a different first PREFIXLEN bytes. Serialization is a
; prefix code, so no leaf starts with two assets' complete prefixes,
; and disclaiming a genuine member always fails. This is what lets
; two assets share a transaction, each run partitioning the odd
; outputs into its own members and proven foreigners.
def (DISCLAIM PREFIX V LEAF IPK PATH PAR SPK) (if (notall (= V 0xc2) (= (substr LEAF 0 (PREFIXLEN)) PREFIX)) (TAPROOT PAR (HASHTAPLEAF V LEAF) PATH IPK (CHECKTAPSPK SPK)) (x "cat: disclaimed member"))
def (ODISCLAIM PREFIX C SPK) (DISCLAIM PREFIX (h C) (h (t C)) (h (t (t C))) (h (t (t (t C)))) (t (t (t (t C)))) SPK)

; one claimed odd output: the claim must rebuild the output's
; scriptPubKey, then its amount joins the sum. MEMBER raises on a
; mismatch, the refusal arm closes the shape for the reader.
def (OSUM PREFIX C J SUM) (if (MEMBER PREFIX (h C) (t C) (tx (rc J 21))) (+ SUM (tx (rc J 20))) (x "cat: output claim"))

; dispatch one output entry: a (nil SINNER . PAR) member claim joins
; the sum, a (1 V LEAF IPK PATH . PAR) disclaimer proves the output
; foreign and leaves the sum alone
def (OSUM2 PREFIX C J SUM) (if (h C) (if (ODISCLAIM PREFIX (t C) (tx (rc J 21))) SUM (x "cat: disclaim")) (OSUM PREFIX (t C) J SUM))

; scan every output: each odd output consumes one entry, claimed or
; disclaimed, even outputs pass through unclaimed, and the entry
; list must end exactly with the odd outputs
def (OUTSCAN PREFIX J N CL SUM) (if (= J N) (if CL (x "cat: leftover output claims") SUM) (if (ODD8 (tx (rc J 20))) (if CL (OUTSCAN PREFIX (+ J 1) N (t CL) (OSUM2 PREFIX (h CL) J SUM)) (x "cat: unclaimed odd output")) (OUTSCAN PREFIX (+ J 1) N CL SUM)))

; one input claim (IDX SINNER . PAR), indices normalized and
; strictly increasing so no input is counted twice, bounded by the
; input count, and every claimed input must be an odd member. An out
; of range index also raises through the introspection op itself.
; SEEN tracks whether the executing input claimed itself.
def (INCLAIM2 PREFIX I LS LP PREV CL SUM SEEN) (if (all (< PREV I) (< I (tx 2)) (ODD8 (tx (rc I 15))) (MEMBER PREFIX LS LP (tx (rc I 16)))) (INCLAIM PREFIX I CL (+ SUM (tx (rc I 15))) (any SEEN (= I (tx 4)))) (x "cat: input claim"))
def (INCLAIM PREFIX PREV CL SUM SEEN) (if CL (INCLAIM2 PREFIX (+ (h (h CL)) 0) (h (t (h CL))) (t (t (h CL))) PREV (t CL) SUM SEEN) (if SEEN SUM (x "cat: own input not claimed")))

; the grandparent's output at cursor C is an odd member, proven by
; the lineage claim's SINNER and parity. The lazy if keeps the
; raising member rebuild off outputs the parity already refuses.
def (SPENTMEM PREFIX LS LP P2 C) (if (ODD8 (substr P2 C (+ C 8))) (MEMBER PREFIX LS LP (substr P2 (+ C 9) (+ C 9 (RD1 P2 (+ C 8))))))

; the grandparent's output named by outpoint index OPN is an odd
; member. C is the position of P2's output count byte. The index
; bound keeps the OUTPOS recursion below the RD1 ceiling, a witness
; supplied counter must never drive an unbounded walk.
def (LOUT PREFIX LS LP P2 OPN C) (if (all (< -1 OPN) (< OPN (RD1 P2 C))) (SPENTMEM PREFIX LS LP P2 (OUTPOS P2 (+ C 1) OPN)))

; only a P2 that hashes to the outpoint's txid is parsed at all, the
; lazy if keeps every cursor walk on hash verified bytes
def (ANCESTRY2 PREFIX LS LP P2 OP) (if (= (hash256 P2) (substr OP 0 32)) (LOUT PREFIX LS LP P2 (+ (substr OP 32 36) 0) (SKIPINS P2 5 (RD1 P2 4))))

; the parent's input J spent an odd member output, proven by
; revealing the grandparent transaction. J is witness supplied, so
; it is bounded by the input count and re-encoded minimally before
; it drives SKIPINS, whose countdown ends on the empty atom: a
; non-minimal zero would pass the numeric bound yet never count
; down.
def (ANCESTRY PREFIX LS LP P P2 J) (if (all (< -1 J) (< J (RD1 P 4))) (ANCESTRY2 PREFIX LS LP P2 (PREVOUTAT P (SKIPINS P 5 (+ J 0)))))

; the ancestry claim: my parent transaction, already pinned to
; (tx 11) at the entry, held a member input. That input's own run
; verified every odd output of the parent, including me, so one
; exhibited member carries the induction.
def (LINEAGE PREFIX PROOF PROOF2 LC) (if PROOF2 (ANCESTRY PREFIX (h (t LC)) (t (t LC)) PROOF PROOF2 (h LC)))

; the issuance path: the revealed program must tree hash to the
; committed TAILHASH, then its verdict over the argument tree
; (DELTA PROOF . TS), DELTA at 2 and PROOF at 5, decides
def (RUNTAIL TR TS DELTA PROOF) (if (= (SHA256TREE TR) (TAILHASH)) (a TR (rc (rc TS PROOF) DELTA)) (x "cat: tail hash"))

; a zero delta with a proven lineage needs no issuance program, any
; other spend stands or falls with the revealed one
def (DELTAOK PREFIX DELTA PROOF PROOF2 LC TAILR TAILS) (if TAILR (RUNTAIL TAILR TAILS DELTA PROOF) (all (notall DELTA) (LINEAGE PREFIX PROOF PROOF2 LC)))

; the main entry. all is eager, so every check runs and one refusal
; closes: the committed PREFIXLEN pins the revealed split, the
; rebuilt leaf must be the executing leaf, my own amount is odd, the
; parent reveal is pinned before either branch reads it, the
; transaction conserves or the issuance program approves, and the
; holder's inner program authorizes.
def (CAT2 PREFIX SINNERME ICLAIMS OCLAIMS PROOF PROOF2 LC TAILR TAILS IARGS INNER) (if (all (= (strlen PREFIX) (PREFIXLEN)) (= (HASHLEAF PREFIX SINNERME) (tx 6)) (ODD8 (tx 15)) (= (hash256 PROOF) (tx 11)) (DELTAOK PREFIX (- (OUTSCAN PREFIX 0 (tx 3) OCLAIMS 0) (INCLAIM PREFIX -1 ICLAIMS 0 0)) PROOF PROOF2 LC TAILR TAILS) (a INNER IARGS)) 1 (x "cat: invalid spend"))

; the wrapper entry BODY compiles from: the leaf applies BODY to
; (W . INNER), W the witness environment element documented in the
; header and INNER the holder's quoted inner program riding the leaf
def (CAT W INNER) (CAT2 (h (h (h W))) (t (h (h W))) (h (t (h W))) (t (t (h W))) (h (h (t W))) (t (h (t W))) (h (h (t (t W)))) (t (h (t (t W)))) (h (t (t (t W)))) (t (t (t (t W)))) INNER)

; --- end committed program ---

